    "fatGrams": 50.9
  },
  "ingredients": [
    "6 tablespoon almond flour",
    "2 large egg",
    "1 tablespoon erythritol",
    "1/4 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1/2 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "2 tablespoon cream cheese",
    "1 tablespoon erythritol",
    "1 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "2 teaspoon leftover batter",
    "1/4 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Crack an egg into a mixing bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01630.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add your erythritol and mix it together very well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01631.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add your almond flour and cinnamon to the mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01633.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix this together well until there's no lumps. Then, add your second egg, vanilla, and baking soda. Mix again until batter is smooth.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01634.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn your waffle iron on and wait for it to get hot. You need to spray it down with some sort of non-stick spray if it isn't non-stick. Fill your waffle maker with the batter and let it cook. Save a little bit of the batter (about 2 tsp.) to go into the filling. While waffles cook, to a small bowl add the cream cheese and erythritol.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01635.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Next add the heavy cream, cinnamon, and a little bit of batter. Mix it together very well, so that everything is combined. I like to leave small lumps of cream cheese in to change the texture as I'm eating the cinnamon roll waffle.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01636.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once your waffle is finished cooking, cut it into sized pieces you want. Add the filling to each piece, so that you can make a sandwich.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/DSC01638.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandwich them together and enjoy! The waffles are a tad dry, so you need some sort of filling to thoroughly enjoy them.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-cinnamon-roll-waffle/#wprm-recipe-50629-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
